# Event Flyer Scrape → Event Details + Media Upload

## Overview

When the user provides **local flyer images** and asks to create events, **do not** hand-enter them in the admin UI. Use a **one-off Node script** that:

1. **Scrapes** title, date, time, venue, caption, contacts, and admission from the image (vision + Tesseract OCR).
2. **POSTs** a row to backend `event_details` (`/api/event-details`).
3. **Uploads** the flyer as event media (`POST /api/event-medias/upload`) with flyer + hero flags.

This is **append-only** by default (skip create if the same title already exists; still upload media). Do **not** change app server actions or proxy handlers for one-off tenant seeds.

## Canonical Scripts

| Script | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| [`scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs`](mdc:scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs) | **Preferred for any tenant.** Append-only. One poster via flags or a JSON spec. Tenant is `MOSC_TENANT_ID` or `NEXT_PUBLIC_TENANT_ID`. |
| [`scripts/lib/seedEventFromFlyer.mjs`](mdc:scripts/lib/seedEventFromFlyer.mjs) | Shared create + hero upload used by the CLI and tenant catalogs. |
| [`scripts/seed-kcnj-event-from-flyer.mjs`](mdc:scripts/seed-kcnj-event-from-flyer.mjs) | KCNJ catalog only. Calls the shared seeder. Does not invent a spec for an unknown image. |
| [`scripts/seed-mcefee-events-from-charity-site.mjs`](mdc:scripts/seed-mcefee-events-from-charity-site.mjs) | **Destructive.** Deletes all tenant events + media, then recreates from a hardcoded list. Use only when the user asks to replace the whole catalog. |
| [`scripts/mosc-in-migration/migration-api-lib.mjs`](mdc:scripts/mosc-in-migration/migration-api-lib.mjs) | Service JWT, `apiFetch`, `API_BASE_URL`, `TENANT_ID` from `.env.local`. `MOSC_TENANT_ID` overrides the env tenant without editing `.env.local`. |

```bash
# Any project. Run inside that repo so .env.local supplies API + JWT + tenant.
# Override tenant when this checkout's .env.local is a different site:
#   $env:MOSC_TENANT_ID="keralacenter_org_9"

node scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs --help

node scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs --spec scripts/flyers/my-event.json --event-type-id 13

node scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs --image C:\path\poster.png --title "Event title" --start-date 2026-10-09 --end-date 2026-10-09 --start-time 18:00:00 --end-time 23:00:00 --location "Venue" --admission ticketed --registration-required --external-url https://example.com/register --event-type-id 13
```

`--event-type-id` or `EVENT_TYPE_ID` is required. Ids are per tenant (on keralacenter_org_9, `13` is Cultural Festival). Do not assume `13` on another tenant.

Requires `.env.local`: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_TENANT_ID`, `API_JWT_USER` / `API_JWT_PASS`.

## Process (agent checklist)

1. **Confirm images exist** on disk.
2. **Scrape pixels** — read the image in-chat (vision) **and** run Tesseract when installed:
   ```powershell
   & "C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe" "<image>" stdout -l eng --psm 6
   ```
   Override binary with `TESSERACT_PATH`. OCR is noisy on illustrated flyers — prefer vision for title/date/venue; use OCR to confirm phones, schedule boxes, age groups.
3. **Pass scraped fields** to `scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs` (flags or a JSON spec). Do not invent dates. A tenant catalog such as `seed-kcnj-event-from-flyer.mjs` is only for flyers already listed in that file. If the flyer has only a month range, follow the MCEFEE last-weekend-of-month convention in the charity-site script.
4. **Copy** the flyer under `public/images/<tenant>/events/` for a local reference.
5. **Create** via `POST /api/event-details` with service JWT + `X-Tenant-ID` (`apiFetch` from migration-api-lib). Include required timestamps (`createdAt`, `updatedAt`), `eventType: { id }`, `tenantId`, `timezone: 'America/New_York'`.
6. **Upload** multipart to `{API_BASE_URL}/api/event-medias/upload?...` (direct backend, not `/api/proxy`). Use `node:buffer` `File`. ASCII-safe filename/title (S3 signing fails on unicode).
7. **Idempotency:** `GET /api/event-details?title.equals=...&size=5`. If found, **skip POST**; still upload media.

## Field mapping from flyer

| Flyer text | `event_details` field | Notes |
|------------|----------------------|--------|
| Event name | `title` | Exact wording from flyer |
| Tagline | `caption` | Short |
| Body + sponsors + contacts | `description` | One string; include schedule/rules/phones |
| Date | `startDate` / `endDate` | `YYYY-MM-DD` |
| Door / start–end | `startTime` / `endTime` | Prefer `HH:mm:ss` |
| Address | `location` | Full venue + street + city |
| Tickets vs free | `admissionType` | `'ticketed'` or `'free'` only |
| Contest / age groups | `isCompetitionEvent` | `true` for competitions |
| “Register by …” | `isRegistrationRequired` | `true` when flyer requires signup |
| Homepage promo | `isFeaturedEvent` + `featuredEventPriorityRanking` | Lower number = higher rank |

Also set: `isActive: true`, `paymentFlowMode: 'STRIPE_ONLY'`, `donationMetadata` JSON (`isFundraiserEvent` / `isCharityEvent`), `fromEmail` for that tenant when the flyer or site publishes one (e.g. `contactus@keralacenter.org`). Registration links go in `externalTicketUrl` (`--external-url`) together with `isRegistrationRequired`.

## Media upload query flags

```javascript
eventFlyer: 'true',
isHeroImage: 'true',
isActiveHeroImage: 'true',
isHomePageHeroImage: 'true',
isFeaturedEventImage: String(!!spec.isFeaturedEvent),
isFeaturedImage: String(!!spec.isFeaturedEvent),
isPublic: 'true',
isEventManagementOfficialDocument: 'false',
displayOrder: '0',
tenantId: TENANT_ID,
eventId: String(eventId),
```

Headers: `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`, `X-Tenant-ID: <tenant>`. Body: `FormData` with `file`.

## DO / DON'T

```javascript
// ✅ DO: append-only seed; JWT + X-Tenant-ID; scrape before inventing fields
const existing = await findExistingByTitle(spec.title, token);
if (existing.length) { await uploadHeroImage(existing[0].id, spec.imagePath, spec, token); return; }
await createEvent(spec, token);

// ❌ DON'T: wipe the tenant catalog unless the user asked for a full replace
// ❌ DON'T: POST event_details from a client component or /api/proxy from this script
// ❌ DON'T: skip OCR/vision and guess dates
// ❌ DON'T: send unicode in S3 upload filenames
```

- ✅ Prefer scripts over UI for bulk flyer ingest.
- ✅ Keep `EVENTS[]` as the scraped source of truth (comment which image each row came from).
- ❌ Do not use `seed-mcefee-events-from-charity-site.mjs` for a single new flyer (it deletes everything).

## Tenant reuse

Copy [`scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs`](mdc:scripts/seed-event-from-flyer.mjs), [`scripts/lib/seedEventFromFlyer.mjs`](mdc:scripts/lib/seedEventFromFlyer.mjs), and [`scripts/mosc-in-migration/migration-api-lib.mjs`](mdc:scripts/mosc-in-migration/migration-api-lib.mjs) into a frontend that does not have them. Run the script from that frontend so `.env.local` selects the tenant. Set `MOSC_TENANT_ID` only when you must target a different tenant than the file’s `NEXT_PUBLIC_TENANT_ID`. Look up that tenant’s event type id before posting. Keep tenant-specific catalogs (such as the KCNJ `EVENTS[]` list) as data that calls `seedFlyers`, not as a second uploader.

